From: Vincenzo Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:44:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0039 a native core for SEARCH, not for latency (5652 passed)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

MEASURED FIRST, on this tree, before a line of C++:

  one CarryEngine.on_candle decision        1.8 us
  decisions the book actually makes         3 per day (the funding clock)
  one 4-year settlement simulation          5 ms (4,500 prints)

The decision path has five orders of magnitude of headroom and the order path
is bounded by a 50-200 ms round trip to Bybit. Nothing in this repository
trades faster because of C++ and nothing ever will; anyone selling that is
selling latency to a book that holds for five days.

What Python IS too slow for is search: which exit rule survives out of sample,
what a maker fill does to the round trip, where impact eats the edge at size,
what the wick does at tick resolution. Those are 10^4-10^7 simulations, and at
5 ms each a morning's question becomes a week.

cpp/carrycore.cpp — one translation unit, no dependencies, a C ABI loaded by
ctypes (no pybind11, no wheel, nothing to install; PyPI is blocked anyway). It
reimplements the settlement simulator AND carry_costs.evaluate_entry gate for
gate, in the same order.

  python      6.23 ms/run     net +29,696.41
  c++         3.18 ms/run     net +29,696.41     difference $0.0000
  sweep       1,440 configurations in 42 ms = 34,056/s, 29 us each
  the same grid in python: 9 s                   212x

A single call is marshalling-bound; the sweep marshals once, which is why it
is the honest number.

THE DIFFERENTIAL TEST IS THE POINT. Six configurations — overlay and acquire,
gated and ungated, three borrow rates, with and without impact — and the build
fails unless every term matches the Python TO THE CENT and the trade counts
match exactly. A fast simulator that disagrees with the slow one is not fast,
it is wrong.

tools/carry_sweep.py uses it and refuses to profit from it: every run records
its SEARCH WIDTH in the registry (a correction that does not know how many
cells were looked at is not a correction), and --best demands an out-of-sample
window, asks the read ledger, names the reads that overlap it, and refuses.
Recorded plainly because hiding it would be worse: the best in-sample cell is
+11.98%/yr against the engine's +7.23%, and it is NOT adopted. That is the
shape of number that cleared funding_carry_fade_btc_v1 and then lost money
forward twice.

The core touches no orders, no venue, no keys, no state and no network; tests
grep for each. The engine, broker and gates stay Python, where correctness
matters and 1.8 us is already free.

Tests first: bot/tests/test_carry_core.py, 28 new. The .so is BUILT, never
committed (.gitignore); no compiler is a skip, never a silent Python fallback
pretending to be fast.

Files: cpp/{carrycore.cpp,carrycore.h,Makefile}, bot/tools/{carry_core,
carry_sweep}.py, bot/tests/test_carry_core.py, bot/docs/human/
{CPP_CORE_0039,INVENTORY}.md, bot/artifacts/hypothesis_registry.json,
README.md, .gitignore

